ing warranty, contract, negligence or strict liability. \nDisclaimer. For industrial use only. Not intended, labeled or packaged for consumer sale or use.\n© 3M 2022. All rights reserved. \n3M, Novec and Fluorinert are trademarks of 3M Company. \n60-5005-0184-0\n03/2022\n-150\n-100\n-50\n0\n50\n100\n150\nDegrees (°C)\nElectronics Materials Solutions Division\n3M Center, Building 224-3N-11\nSt. Paul, MN 55144-1000\nwww.3M.com/novec\n\n---\n\nTitle: 3M™ Novec™ 7100 Engineered Fluid, 272.1 kg (600 lb), 1 Drum\nURL: https://www.3m.com/3M/en_US/p/dc/v000566768/\nPublished: N/A\nAuthor: N/A\nHighlights:\n# 3M™ Novec™ 7100 Engineered Fluid, 272.1 kg (600 lb), 1 Drum\n\n- UPC 00051135451243\n- 3M ID 7010402072\n- 3M Product Number 7100\n- Part Number Novec 7100\n\nChange options\n\n| Maximum Use Temperature (Celsius) | 150 ℃ |\n| --- | --- |\n| Volume (Metric) | 250.035 L |\n| Volume (Imperial) | 55 gal |\n| Net Weight (Imperial) | 600 lb |\n| Net Weight (Metric) | 272 kg |\n| Maximum Use Temperature (Fahrenheit) | 302 ℉ |\n\nNon-flammable\n\nNon-conductive\n\nCompatible with plastics\n\nView more details\n\n###### Frequently viewed resources\n\nTech Data Sheet (PDF, 123KB) View all resources\n\nView legal disclaimer\n\n...\n\n### Details\n\n##### Highlights\n\n- Low surface tension penetrates tight spaces for improved cleaning\n- VOC-exempt solvent (US EPA)\n- Zero ozone depletion potential (ODP)\n- Low global warming potential (GWP)\n- Low toxicity\n- Compatible with plastics\n- Non-conductive\n- Non-flammable\n\n3M™ Novec™ 7100 Engineered Fluid is a proprietary hydrofluoroether (HFE) with unique properties that make it ideal for a broad range of applications and industries, from thermal management in semiconductor fabrication, to immersion cooling in data centers, to solvent cleaning and aerosol formulations. It's non-flammable, has low toxicity, and has a low global warming potential and zero ozone depletion potential, in addition to powerful thermal heat transfer and solvent cleaning performance.\n\n---\n\nTitle: Efficient Cooling. Safe Operation. Sustainable Performance.\nURL: https://www.puretecs.de/images/pdf-en/cooling/tds_AURON%20HFE-7100_EN.pdf\nPublished: N/A\nAuthor: Un-named\nHighlights:\nHFE-7100\n\nCAS 163702-08-7 Dielectric heat transfer fluid\n\n## Efficient Cooling. Safe Operation. Sustainable Performance.\n\n## RODUCT OVERVIEW\n\n## TECHNICAL SPECIFICATIONS\n\nAURON HFE 7100 is an advanced fluorinated ether designed for high-performance thermal management, precision cleaning, and solvent applications. It offers excellent dielectric properties, low viscosity, and strong chemical stability, making it suitable for direct contact cooling of energized components and sensitive materials.\n\n| Appearance | Clear, colourless |\n| --- | --- |\n| Chemical Type | Fluorinated ether |\n| Flash Point | None |\n| Boiling Point | 59°C |\n| Pour Point | -135°C |\n| Critical Temperature | 195°C |\n| Critical Pressure | No information available |\n| Density (25°C) | 1.5 g/ml |\n\nAppearance Clear, colourless Chemical Type Fluorinated ether Flash Point None Boiling Point 59°C Pour Point -135°C Critical Temperature 195°C Critical Pressure No information available Density (25°C) 1.5 g/ml Molecular Weight 250 g/mol\n\n## KEY FEATURES\n\n| Kinematic Viscosity | (25°C) 0.38 cSt |\n| --- | --- |\n| Dynamic Viscosity | 0.57 cP |\n| Surface Tension | 13.6 mN/m |\n| Specific Heat Capacity | 1.18 kJ/(kg·K) |\n| Thermal Conductivity | 0.069 W/(m·K) |\n\n▸ Non-flammable — no flash point ▸ Excellent dielectric properties ▸ Very low-viscosity — High flow efficiency ▸ Low surface tension — superior wetting ▸ High chemical and hydrolysis stability ▸ Fast evaporation / drying capability\n\n| Heat of Vaporization | | 103 | kJ/kg |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Suitable for cooling, cleaning & solvent use ▸ | | | |\n| Expansion Coefficient | | ~0.0017 | K⁻¹ |\n| Vapour Pressure | (25°C) | 28 | kPa |\n\nHeat of Vaporization 103 kJ/kg \nExpansion Coefficient ~0.0017 K⁻¹ \nVapour Pressure (25°C) 28 kPa \nWater Solubility ~ 12 ppm \nn-octanol-water partition \ncoefficient (°C) \n\n## APPLICATIONS\n\nLog Pow: ~ 3.9\n\n▸ Immersion cooling (1-phase systems) ▸ Data center & power electronics cooling ▸ Semiconductor temperature control ▸ Medical industry cooling ▸ Precision cleaning (metal, plastic, resin, dust) ▸ Drying processes (after solvent cleaning) ▸ Diluent for lubricants & specialty chemicals\n\n...\n\nECONOMIC ADVANTAGES & SUSTAINABILITY ▸ Efficient cooling due to low viscosity ▸ Multi-functional (cooling + cleaning + solvent) ▸ Low consumption in drying applications ▸ Long service life with stable performance\n\nELECTRICAL INSULATION ▸ Dielectric strength: > 25 kV (2.54 mm gap) ▸ Dielectric constant: ~7.27 ▸ High resistivity (>10⁸ Ω·cm)\n\nTHERMAL PERFORMANCE ▸ Low viscosity → high heat transfer efficiency ▸ Fast evaporation → efficient cooling & drying ▸ Stable thermal properties across wide temperature range\n\nRecommended operating range (typical) ▸ Approx. -100°C to +50°C\n\n---\n\nTitle: Heat transfer applications using 3M ™ Novec\nURL: http://www.e-pki.com/product/pdf/NOVEC.pdf\nPublished: N/A\nAuthor: N/A\nHighlights:\n## Heat transfer applications using 3M ™ Novec ™\n\nEngineered Fluids Balancing the demand for thermal management performance with worker safety and low environmental impact has never been more important. 3M recognizes your need for a long-term heat transfer fluid with low greenhouse gas emissions and has meticulously engineered the solution – a comprehensive portfolio of 3M ™ Novec ™ Engineered Fluids. You can reduce greenhouse gas emissions by up to 99 percent in your application by replacing perfluorocarbon (PFC) or perfluoropolyether (PFPE) heat transfer fluids with Novec fluids. Now that’s a sustainable solution.\n\n3M ™ Novec ™ Engineered Fluids 7000 649 7100 774 7200 7300 7500 7700\n\nProperties Unit\n\n| Boiling Point | °C | 34 | 49 | 61 | 74 | 76 | 98 | 128 | 167 |\n| --- | --- | -