{"type":"text","timestamp":1792296235058,"sessionID":"ses_eb2e3e793ffeP3gU3LiO0WsJ8Q","part":{"id":"prt_14d2cfe91001wcjgBr3n7UOCTY","messageID":"msg_14d2cb2a8001pPwCOVkNE2bAeP","sessionID":"ses_eb2e3e793ffeP3gU3LiO0WsJ8Q","type":"text","text":"{\"option_title\":\"Force-field error floor for coolant MD: an enlarged C10–C50 benchmark scored against measurement\",\"question\":\"Does GPU Green–Kubo MD of C10–C50 hydrocarbons and esters rank immersion-coolant viscosity and thermal conductivity the way measurements rank them?\",\"hypothesis\":\"Green–Kubo MD with one fixed force field has a chemistry-dependent error floor near 25 percent that more molecules cannot remove [s_ogbomo_res].\",\"compute_axis\":{\"quantity\":\"benchmark molecules scored against measured viscosity and thermal conductivity\",\"unit\":\"molecules\",\"levels\":[8,24,48,120]},\"held_fixed\":[\"temperature 313.15 kelvin and 1 atmosphere\",\"LOPLS-AA force field with the closest prior's public LAMMPS settings [s_zenodo]\",\"250 molecules per simulation box [s_brandt]\",\"2 femtosecond timestep with PME electrostatics\",\"Green–Kubo estimators: three off-diagonal stress components plus heat-flux autocorrelation in the same trajectories\",\"trajectory budget per molecule: 2 ns equilibration plus six 5 ns production replicas\"],\"predictions\":{\"if_lever\":\"At 120 molecules, held-out viscosity error after bias correction falls below 15 percent and rank correlation with measurement exceeds 0.9 [s_ogbomo_res].\",\"if_not\":\"Held-out viscosity error stays above 25 percent and rank correlation below 0.7 at every set size, capping candidate ranking [s_ogbomo_res].\",\"decision_rule\":\"At 120 molecules, if_lever when held-out viscosity MAPE is at most 0.15 and Spearman rank correlation is at least 0.90 for both viscosity and thermal conductivity; if_not when MAPE is at least 0.25 or rank correlation at most 0.70 at every set size; otherwise unsure.\",\"noise_rule\":\"Bootstrap the molecules with 1000 resamples for 95 percent intervals on MAPE and rank correlation; a difference is real only if its interval excludes the decision threshold, and each molecule's replica standard error must be below 0.20.\",\"expected\":\"if_not\",\"expected_why\":\"Published LOPLS-AA Green–Kubo runs already show chemistry-dependent errors of tens of percent that more sampling cannot remove [s_ogbomo_res].\"},\"compute_tested\":\"yes\",\"compute_tested_why\":\"The test varies the number of benchmark molecules from 8 to 120, which is exactly the work more parallel GPUs buy; per-molecule trajectory length is held fixed.\",\"scored_against\":\"Measured dynamic viscosity and thermal conductivity at 40 degrees Celsius from the public 835-molecule C10–C50 reference set compiled from Landolt–Börnstein and NIST Chemistry WebBook [s_ogbomo_db]; commercial single-phase coolant data sheets give property bands only [s_ef_visc].\",\"arms\":[{\"id\":\"a_base\",\"what\":\"8 molecules, 2 ns equilibration, three 2 ns replicas: today's small-set practice, scored identically [s_ogbomo_md]\"},{\"id\":\"a_core\",\"what\":\"48 molecules at the full protocol: 2 ns equilibration and six 5 ns replicas each\"},{\"id\":\"a_ext\",\"what\":\"120 molecules at the full protocol\"},{\"id\":\"a_long\",\"what\":\"12 of the 48 molecules re-run with six 15 ns replicas, to separate trajectory length from set size\"}],\"baseline\":{\"what\":\"Current practice: Green–Kubo MD on eight representative C10–C50 molecules with one force field [s_ogbomo_md]\",\"value\":8,\"source_id\":\"s_ogbomo_md\"},\"anchor\":{\"what\":\"Repeat the published eight-molecule Green–Kubo run first: density within 4% for seven molecules and thermal conductivity over-predicted for all eight [s_ogbomo_res].\",\"published_value\":\"density error 4% or less on 7 of 8 molecules at 40 °C\",\"tolerance\":\"same bias signs for viscosity and thermal conductivity; density error within 4 percentage points of the published error; per-molecule viscosity within 20% of the reference value\",\"source_id\":\"s_ogbomo_res\",\"independent_code\":\"the prior's public LAMMPS decks and Green–Kubo analysis script, Zenodo 10.5281/zenodo.21824121 [s_zenodo]\"},\"checks\":[\"Density within 2% of the reference value before any transport property is scored\",\"The three off-diagonal stress components of the viscosity agree within the replica spread\",\"Green–Kubo integral plateau time is shorter than one tenth of the production length [s_maginn]\",\"NVE energy drift of one production run stays below 0.01% of the total energy\",\"Viscosity units audited as millipascal-seconds against the reference range 1 to 50 mPa·s [s_ogbomo_range]\",\"Two molecules re-run with different seeds agree within the replica standard error [s_livecoms]\"],\"phases\":[{\"id\":\"p_local\",\"what\":\"Assemble the LOPLS-AA LAMMPS protocol from the public decks and validate the scoring and noise rules on synthetic Green–Kubo data using pilot/cost_and_noise_check.py\",\"gate\":{\"on\":\"rank_fp_rate\",\"op\":\"<=\",\"value\":0.08,\"else\":\"fix the scoring code before any GPU spend\"}},{\"id\":\"p_bench\",\"what\":\"GPU pilot: 4 molecules with 3 replicas of 8 ns; measure throughput, Green–Kubo plateau time and replica spread\",\"gate\":{\"on\":\"throughput_ns_day\",\"op\":\">=\",\"value\":150,\"else\":\"drop the extension tier and re-plan with 48 molecules at 3 replicas\"}},{\"id\":\"p_anchor\",\"what\":\"Run the prior's eight molecules and compare with their published values and the reference measurements\",\"gate\":{\"on\":\"eta_anchor_err\",\"op\":\"<=\",\"value\":0.2,\"else\":\"stop and report that the protocol is not trustworthy; make no ranking claim\"}},{\"id\":\"p_core\",\"what\":\"Benchmark 48 molecules, including the anchor eight, at the fixed protocol\"},{\"id\":\"p_ext\",\"what\":\"Extend the benchmark to 120 molecules\",\"gate\":{\"on\":\"eta_se_frac\",\"op\":\"<=\",\"value\":0.2,\"else\":\"spend the extension money on longer trajectories for the 48 core molecules instead of new molecules\"}},{\"id\":\"p_score\",\"what\":\"Score error distributions, held-out bias correction and rank correlation at 8, 24, 48 and 120 molecules; write the report\"}],\"numbers\":[{\"id\":\"n_ref_molecules\",\"name\":\"molecules in the public reference set\",\"unit\":\"molecules\",\"basis\":\"CITED\",\"value\":835,\"source_id\":\"s_ogbomo_db\",\"quote\":\"We compile a database of approximately 4,700 critically evaluated reference values for the density, viscosity, and thermal conductivity of 835 unique organic molecules in the C10–C50 range.\",\"page_setting\":\"reference dataset of measured density, viscosity and thermal conductivity at 40 and 100 °C\"},{\"id\":\"eta_min_mpas\",\"name\":\"lowest reference viscosity in scope\",\"unit\":\"mPa·s\",\"basis\":\"CITED\",\"value\":1,\"source_id\":\"s_ogbomo_range\",\"quote\":\"Only molecules with a dynamic viscosity of approximately 1–50 mPa·s at 40 °C were included, because this is the range accessible to equilibrium molecular dynamics (EMD).\",\"page_setting\":\"molecule inclusion criterion of the reference dataset at 40 °C\"},{\"id\":\"eta_max_mpas\",\"name\":\"highest reference viscosity in scope\",\"unit\":\"mPa·s\",\"basis\":\"CITED\",\"value\":50,\"source_id\":\"s_ogbomo_range\",\"quote\":\"Only molecules with a dynamic viscosity of approximately 1–50 mPa·s at 40 °C were included, because this is the range accessible to equilibrium molecular dynamics (EMD).\",\"page_setting\":\"molecule inclusion criterion of the reference dataset at 40 °C\"},{\"id\":\"n_mol_per_box\",\"name\":\"molecules per simulation box\",\"unit\":\"molecules\",\"basis\":\"CITED\",\"value\":250,\"source_id\":\"s_brandt\",\"quote\":\"we verify that the viscosity of molecular liquids is not influenced by finite size effects down to systems as small as 250 molecules.\",\"page_setting\":\"Green–Kubo and OrthoBoXY viscosity of 15 molecular liquids, multi-size study\"},{\"id\":\"atoms_per_mol_avg\",\"name\":\"average atoms per benchmark molecule\",\"unit\":\"atoms\",\"basis\":\"DERIVED\",\"expr\":\"(32 + 152) / 2\"},{\"id\":\"atoms_per_box\",\"name\":\"atoms per simulation box\",\"unit\":\"atoms\",\"basis\":\"DERIVED\",\"expr\":\"n_mol_per_box * atoms_per_mol_avg\"},{\"id\":\"n_gpus\",\"name\":\"GPUs on the rented instance\",\"unit\":\"GPUs\",\"basis\":\"CITED\",\"value\":8,\"source_id\":\"s_lambda\",\"quote\":\"Instances pricing (8x): NVIDIA A100 SXM | VRAM/GPU: 40 GB | vCPUs: 124 | RAM: 1800 GiB | STORAGE: 5.8 TiB SSD | PRICE/GPU/HR*: $1.99\",\"page_setting\":\"Lambda on-demand 8-GPU A100 SXM 40 GB instance\"},{\"id\":\"a100x8_usd_gpu_h\",\"name\":\"price per GPU-hour, 8x A100 SXM 40 GB\",\"unit\":\"USD/GPU-hour\",\"basis\":\"CITED\",\"value\":1.99,\"source_id\":\"s_lambda\",\"quote\":\"Instances pricing (8x): NVIDIA A100 SXM | VRAM/GPU: 40 GB | vCPUs: 124 | RAM: 1800 GiB | STORAGE: 5.8 TiB SSD | PRICE/GPU/HR*: $1.99\",\"page_setting\":\"Lambda on-demand instance pricing read 2026-10-18\"},{\"id\":\"a6000_usd_gpu_h\",\"name\":\"price per GPU-hour, 1x A6000\",\"unit\":\"USD/GPU-hour\",\"basis\":\"CITED\",\"value\":1.09,\"source_id\":\"s_lambda_a6000\",\"quote\":\"Instances pricing (1x): NVIDIA A6000 | VRAM/GPU: 48 GB | vCPUs: 14 | RAM: 100 GiB | STORAGE: 512 GiB SSD | PRICE/GPU/HR*: $1.09\",\"page_setting\":\"Lambda on-demand instance pricing read 2026-10-18\"},{\"id\":\"throughput_ns_day\",\"name\":\"assumed MD throughput per GPU\",\"unit\":\"ns/day\",\"basis\":\"PROXY\",\"value\":250,\"source_id\":\"s_amber\",\"quote\":\"1 x A100 GPU:      |         ns/day =    611.08\",\"page_setting\":\"Amber JAC_PRODUCTION_NVE benchmark, 23,558 atoms, PME, 2 fs timestep, one A100 GPU\",\"differs_in\":[\"Amber pmemd.cuda rather than LAMMPS\",\"protein in water rather than neat organic liquid\",\"no per-step stress-tensor autocorrelation accumulation\",\"we take 250 ns/day as a safety factor of about 2.4 under the 611 ns/day figure\"],\"measured_by\":\"p_bench\"},{\"id\":\"throughput_gate_min\",\"name\":\"minimum acceptable measured throughput\",\"unit\":\"ns/day\",\"basis\":\"DESIGN\",\"value\":150},{\"id\":\"n_replicas\",\"name\":\"independent production replicas per molecule\",\"unit\":\"replicas\",\"basis\":\"DESIGN\",\"value\":6},{\"id\":\"t_eq_ns\",\"name\":\"equilibration time per molecule\",\"unit\":\"ns\",\"basis\":\"DESIGN\",\"value\":2},{\"id\":\"t_prod_ns\",\"name\":\"production length per replica\",\"unit\":\"ns\",\"basis\":\"DESIGN\",\"value\":5},{\"id\":\"ns_per_mol\",\"name\":\"trajectory nanoseconds per molecule\",\"unit\":\"ns\",\"basis\":\"DERIVED\",\"expr\":\"t_eq_ns + n_replicas * t_prod_ns\"},{\"id\":\"gpu_h_per_mol\",\"name\":\"GPU-hours per molecule\",\"unit\":\"GPU-hour\",\"basis\":\"DERIVED\",\"expr\":\"24 * ns_per_mol / throughput_ns_day\"},{\"id\":\"mol_usd\",\"name\":\"dollars per molecule at design throughput\",\"unit\":\"USD\",\"basis\":\"DERIVED\",\"expr\":\"gpu_h_per_mol * a100x8_usd_gpu_h\"},{\"id\":\"n_mol_anchor\",\"name\":\"anchor molecules from the prior\",\"unit\":\"molecules\",\"basis\":\"DESIGN\",\"value\":8},{\"id\":\"n_mol_core\",\"name\":\"molecules in the core benchmark\",\"unit\":\"molecules\",\"basis\":\"DESIGN\",\"value\":48},{\"id\":\"n_mol_total\",\"name\":\"molecules in the full benchmark\",\"unit\":\"molecules\",\"basis\":\"DESIGN\",\"value\":120},{\"id\":\"n_mol_ext\",\"name\":\"molecules added in the extension tier\",\"unit\":\"molecules\",\"basis\":\"DERIVED\",\"expr\":\"n_mol_total - n_mol_core\"},{\"id\":\"pilot_ns\",\"name\":\"pilot trajectory nanoseconds\",\"unit\":\"ns\",\"basis\":\"DESIGN\",\"value\":150},{\"id\":\"gib_store\",\"name\":\"filesystem size reserved\",\"unit\":\"GiB\",\"basis\":\"DESIGN\",\"value\":150},{\"id\":\"store_usd\",\"name\":\"filesystem cost for one month\",\"unit\":\"USD\",\"basis\":\"DERIVED\",\"expr\":\"gib_store * fs_usd_gib_month\"},{\"id\":\"rerun_usd\",\"name\":\"re-run allotment\",\"unit\":\"USD\",\"basis\":\"DESIGN\",\"value\":120},{\"id\":\"mape_lever_max\",\"name\":\"held-out viscosity error for if_lever\",\"unit\":\"fraction\",\"basis\":\"DESIGN\",\"value\":0.15},{\"id\":\"rho_lever_min\",\"name\":\"rank correlation for if_lever\",\"unit\":\"fraction\",\"basis\":\"DESIGN\",\"value\":0.9},{\"id\":\"mape_not_min\",\"name\":\"held-out viscosity error for if_not\",\"unit\":\"fraction\",\"basis\":\"DESIGN\",\"value\":0.25},{\"id\":\"rho_not_max\",\"name\":\"rank correlation for if_not\",\"unit\":\"fraction\",\"basis\":\"DESIGN\",\"value\":0.7},{\"id\":\"eta_anchor_err\",\"name\":\"expected worst anchor viscosity error\",\"unit\":\"fraction\",\"basis\":\"GUESS\",\"value\":0.25,\"rests_on\":\"the prior reports small LOPLS-AA viscosity errors for hydrocarbons and consistent under-prediction for oxygenates, so 25 percent sits mid-range of published per-molecule force-field errors\",\"measured_by\":\"p_anchor\"},{\"id\":\"eta_se_frac\",\"name\":\"expected replica standard error of viscosity\",\"unit\":\"fraction\",\"basis\":\"GUESS\",\"value\":0.15,\"rests_on\":\"published practice that five to ten Green–Kubo replicas of a few nanoseconds give a standard error of order ten to twenty percent\",\"measured_by\":\"p_bench\"},{\"id\":\"mape_core\",\"name\":\"expected viscosity error over 48 molecules\",\"unit\":\"fraction\",\"basis\":\"GUESS\",\"value\":0.3,\"rests_on\":\"published force-field viscosity errors for alkanes and esters of roughly twenty to fifty percent\",\"measured_by\":\"p_core\"},{\"id\":\"rank_fp_rate\",\"name\":\"false-positive rate of the rank rule\",\"unit\":\"fraction\",\"basis\":\"GUESS\",\"value\":0.05,\"rests_on\":\"bootstrap rank tests at this sample size usually reject a true null about five times in a hundred\",\"measured_by\":\"p_local\"},{\"id\":\"ns_total\",\"name\":\"trajectory nanoseconds bought\",\"unit\":\"ns\",\"basis\":\"DERIVED\",\"expr\":\"n_mol_total * ns_per_mol\"},{\"id\":\"replica_runs\",\"name\":\"independent replica runs bought\",\"unit\":\"runs\",\"basis\":\"DERIVED\",\"expr\":\"n_mol_total * n_replicas\"}],\"cost\":{\"rates\":[{\"id\":\"r_a100x8\",\"gpu\":\"NVIDIA A100 SXM\",\"gpu_memory_gb\":40,\"n_gpus\":8,\"per_gpu_usd_h\":1.99},{\"id\":\"r_a6000x1\",\"gpu\":\"NVIDIA A6000\",\"gpu_memory_gb\":48,\"n_gpus\":1,\"per_gpu_usd_h\":1.09}],\"lines\":[{\"id\":\"l_dry\",\"phase\":\"p_local\",\"what\":\"Build LAMMPS with LOPLS-AA from the public decks, dry-run one molecule for 100 ps, run the synthetic Green–Kubo scoring check\",\"kind\":\"work\",\"rate\":\"r_a6000x1\",\"hours\":4,\"need\":\"time box; work inside not estimated\"},{\"id\":\"l_bench\",\"phase\":\"p_bench\",\"what\":\"Pilot: 4 molecules with 3 replicas of 8 ns, measuring throughput and Green–Kubo plateau\",\"kind\":\"work\",\"rate\":\"r_a100x8\",\"hours\":\"ceil(24 * pilot_ns / (throughput_ns_day * n_gpus))\"},{\"id\":\"l_core\",\"phase\":\"p_core\",\"what\":\"Core benchmark of 48 molecules at the fixed protocol\",\"kind\":\"work\",\"rate\":\"r_a100x8\",\"hours\":\"ceil(24 * n_mol_core * ns_per_mol / (throughput_ns_day * n_gpus))\"},{\"id\":\"l_ext\",\"phase\":\"p_ext\",\"what\":\"Extension to 120 molecules at the fixed protocol\",\"kind\":\"work\",\"rate\":\"r_a100x8\",\"hours\":\"ceil(24 * n_mol_ext * ns_per_mol / (throughput_ns_day * n_gpus))\"},{\"id\":\"l_score\",\"phase\":\"p_score\",\"what\":\"Scoring, held-out bias correction, rank analysis and report writing\",\"kind\":\"work\",\"rate\":\"r_a6000x1\",\"hours\":6,\"need\":\"time box; analysis work not estimated\"},{\"id\":\"l_store\",\"phase\":\"p_score\",\"what\":\"Filesystem for decks, correlation data and reduced results\",\"kind\":\"storage\",\"usd\":\"gib_store * fs_usd_gib_month\"},{\"id\":\"l_rerun\",\"phase\":\"p_score\",\"what\":\"Re-run allotment for molecules whose plateau is not reached or whose replica spread exceeds 0.20\",\"kind\":\"allotment\",\"usd\":\"rerun_usd\",\"condition\":\"only molecules failing the plateau or replica-spread checks\"},{\"id\":\"l_long_traj\",\"phase\":\"p_ext\",\"what\":\"Stretch: 12 molecules re-run with six 15 ns replicas to separate trajectory length from set size\",\"kind\":\"work\",\"rate\":\"r_a100x8\",\"hours\":\"ceil(24 * 12 * (t_eq_ns + n_replicas * 15) / (throughput_ns_day * n_gpus))\",\"optional\":true,\"instead_of\":[\"l_ext\"],\"condition\":\"phase p_bench shows Green–Kubo plateau times longer than 0.5 ns\"}],\"scenarios\":[{\"id\":\"sc_slow\",\"what\":\"Measured throughput is half the proxy: shrink the benchmark rather than overspend\",\"set\":{\"throughput_ns_day\":120,\"n_mol_total\":60,\"rerun_usd\":60}},{\"id\":\"sc_long\",\"what\":\"Replica spread too wide: buy longer runs on fewer molecules\",\"set\":{\"n_replicas\":10,\"t_prod_ns\":8,\"n_mol_total\":60}}],\"yields\":[\"n_mol_total\",\"ns_total\",\"replica_runs\"],\"spend_cap_usd\":1000,\"total_stated\":940.34},\"full_scale\":[{\"id\":\"fs_all835\",\"what\":\"Score all 835 reference molecules at 40 °C with the same protocol\",\"usd\":\"n_ref_molecules * mol_usd\",\"ratio_to\":\"n_mol_total\"},{\"id\":\"fs_two_temp\",\"what\":\"Repeat the 120-molecule benchmark at 100 °C as well\",\"usd\":\"n_mol_total * mol_usd * 2\",\"ratio_to\":\"n_mol_total\"}],\"outside_budget\":[{\"what\":\"local shared-machine CPU time for protocol assembly and scoring code\",\"qty\":20,\"unit\":\"hours\"},{\"what\":\"human time for setup, curation and writing\",\"qty\":10,\"unit\":\"hours\"},{\"what\":\"public reference dataset and prior's LAMMPS decks, downloaded free of charge [s_zenodo]\",\"qty\":1,\"unit\":\"download\"}],\"restructuring\":{\"sequential_part\":\"One molecule needs equilibration, then six runs, then averaging — three steps; different molecules never wait on each other.\",\"method\":\"none\"},\"scope_gap\":[\"Proprietary commercial blends such as ElectroCool or Novec are not simulated; their data sheets give property bands only [s_ef_visc]\",\"Dielectric constant, flash point and heat capacity are not part of the scored test\",\"Only LOPLS-AA is tested; other force fields may show different error floors\",\"Viscosities above 50 mPa·s at 40 °C are outside the accessible reference range [s_ogbomo_range]\"],\"novelty\":{\"closest_prior\":\"Ogbomo et al. 2026 ran Green–Kubo MD for viscosity and thermal conductivity of eight C10–C50 molecules at 40 °C against measurement [s_ogbomo_md].\",\"closest_source_id\":\"s_ogbomo_md\",\"prior_max_level\":8,\"left_open\":\"Whether the error is a correctable bias or a random floor that caps ranking, and how rank agreement holds over hundreds of molecules [s_ogbomo_db].\",\"decides\":\"partly\",\"searched\":true},\"limits\":[\"Shows transport-property error only at 40 °C for pure liquids between 1 and 50 mPa·s, not blends or sold coolants.\",\"Cannot show ranking behaviour beyond 120 molecules.\"],\"test_summary\":\"One LAMMPS LOPLS-AA Green–Kubo protocol at 40 °C, six five-nanosecond replicas per molecule, run on 8, 24, 48 then 120 molecules from the public 835-molecule reference set, scored only against measured viscosity and thermal conductivity [s_ogbomo_db].\",\"sources\":[{\"id\":\"s_ogbomo_db\",\"url\":\"https://spiral.imperial.ac.uk/entities/publication/9423c271-1953-481c-8e8d-88eeb67e2535\",\"quote\":\"We compile a database of approximately 4,700 critically evaluated reference values for the density, viscosity, and thermal conductivity of 835 unique organic molecules in the C10–C50 range.\",\"supports\":\"the measured reference set used for scoring, its size and chemical range\"},{\"id\":\"s_ogbomo_md\",\"url\":\"https://spiral.imperial.ac.uk/entities/publication/9423c271-1953-481c-8e8d-88eeb67e2535\",\"quote\":\"Equilibrium molecular dynamics (EMD) simulations of eight representative molecules reproduce density accurately but show systematic, chemistry-dependent force-field errors for the viscosity and thermal conductivity.\",\"supports\":\"the closest prior work and the baseline arm of eight molecules\"},{\"id\":\"s_ogbomo_res\",\"url\":\"https://spiral.imperial.ac.uk/server/api/core/bitstreams/fa07c113-8958-4f1e-a010-0ef2bfc39e17/content\",\"quote\":\"Density is reproduced to within 4% for seven of the eight molecules at 40 °C. Viscosity errors are small for the pure hydrocarbons with LOPLS, but this property is consistently under-predicted for the oxygen-containing molecules; the reference ranking of the fluids is nonetheless largely preserved. Thermal conductivity is over-predicted for every molecule, by amounts that correlate with the density of aliphatic C–H bonds, compressing the reference range and misordering the fluids.\",\"supports\":\"anchor tolerances, the predicted error floor and the if_not expectation\"},{\"id\":\"s_ogbomo_range\",\"url\":\"https://spiral.imperial.ac.uk/server/api/core/bitstreams/fa07c113-8958-4f1e-a010-0ef2bfc39e17/content\",\"quote\":\"Only molecules with a dynamic viscosity of approximately 1–50 mPa·s at 40 °C were included, because this is the range accessible to equilibrium molecular dynamics (EMD).\",\"supports\":\"the viscosity range the benchmark can cover\"},{\"id\":\"s_zenodo\",\"url\":\"https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21824121\",\"quote\":\"a SMILES-to-LAMMPS builder for the LOPLS-AA force field, the equilibration, production and continuation input decks, and the analysis script that computes density, viscosity and thermal conductivity from Green-Kubo time-decomposition runs.\",\"supports\":\"the independent code the protocol is built from and checked against\"},{\"id\":\"s_brandt\",\"url\":\"https://pubs.aip.org/aip/jcp/article/165/14/144101/3406182/Computing-shear-viscosities-from-molecular\",\"quote\":\"we verify that the viscosity of molecular liquids is not influenced by finite size effects down to systems as small as 250 molecules.\",\"supports\":\"the 250-molecule box size held fixed across all runs\"},{\"id\":\"s_maginn\",\"url\":\"https://magma.geol.ucsb.edu/papers/mol_sim_NaCl_viscosity.pdf\",\"quote\":\"we find that a set of optimal values that effectively trade off accuracy with computational cost are tD = 2ns, tW = 2ps and tS = 10 fs.\",\"supports\":\"the choice of a few nanoseconds per replica and the plateau check\"},{\"id\":\"s_livecoms\",\"url\":\"https://livecomsjournal.org/index.php/livecoms/article/download/v1i1e6324/937/2725\",\"quote\":\"an average of 10 short replicate simulations converges to the same value as a single long simulation. Since these replicates can be performed in parallel, the real time is reduced, although the CPU time may be the same or more.\",\"supports\":\"running replicas as independent parallel jobs and the replica-spread noise rule\"},{\"id\":\"s_ewen_lopls\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5509262/\",\"quote\":\"Conversely, L-OPLS-AA accurately reproduces experimental viscosities (within 15%) under all of the conditions simulated.\",\"supports\":\"choosing LOPLS-AA as the single protocol force field\"},{\"id\":\"s_ewen_chain\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5509262/\",\"quote\":\"It should be noted that the rotational relaxation time, required integration time and ultimately the simulation length, increases by more than an order of magnitude with a relatively modest increase in chain-length (C10 to C16)\",\"supports\":\"the scenario that long chains may need longer trajectories than the fixed five nanoseconds\"},{\"id\":\"s_amber\",\"url\":\"https://ambermd.org/GPUPerformance.php\",\"quote\":\"1 x A100 GPU:      |         ns/day =    611.08\",\"supports\":\"the proxy MD throughput per A100 GPU used in the cost model\"},{\"id\":\"s_lambda\",\"url\":\"https://lambda.ai/pricing\",\"quote\":\"Instances pricing (8x): NVIDIA A100 SXM | VRAM/GPU: 40 GB | vCPUs: 124 | RAM: 1800 GiB | STORAGE: 5.8 TiB SSD | PRICE/GPU/HR*: $1.99\",\"supports\":\"the per-GPU price and GPU count of the main compute rate\"},{\"id\":\"s_lambda_a6000\",\"url\":\"https://lambda.ai/pricing\",\"quote\":\"Instances pricing (1x): NVIDIA A6000 | VRAM/GPU: 48 GB | vCPUs: 14 | RAM: 100 GiB | STORAGE: 512 GiB SSD | PRICE/GPU/HR*: $1.09\",\"supports\":\